{%- comment -%}
  Explainer figure: retraining versus classification by retrieval.
  Drawn from the Computer Networks paper (CESNET-TLS22 and RADCOM data):
  new classes in seconds instead of thousands of seconds, unknown traffic
  flagged by distance. Inline SVG coloured by CSS (_sass/signal/_figures.scss),
  so it follows light and dark mode. Point positions come from a fixed seed.
{%- endcomment -%}
<figure class="note-figure" style="--c: var(--line-traffic)">
  <div class="fig-panels">
    <div class="fig-panel">
      <p class="fig-panel-head">Today: <span>retrain for every new app</span></p>
      <svg class="fig-svg" viewBox="0 0 320 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="cbr-a-t">
        <title id="cbr-a-t">A new app appears, then three steps in a loop: collect labelled traffic, retrain the model for thousands of seconds, redeploy.</title>
        <defs>
          <marker id="fig-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path class="fig-arrowhead" d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <rect class="fig-pill fig-pill-new" x="90" y="8" width="140" height="28" rx="14"/>
        <text class="fig-box-text fig-label-new" x="160" y="27" text-anchor="middle">a new app appears</text>
        <line class="fig-flow" x1="160" y1="38" x2="160" y2="58" marker-end="url(#fig-arrow)"/>
        <rect class="fig-box" x="70" y="62" width="180" height="36" rx="8"/>
        <text class="fig-box-text" x="160" y="85" text-anchor="middle">collect labelled traffic</text>
        <line class="fig-flow" x1="160" y1="100" x2="160" y2="120" marker-end="url(#fig-arrow)"/>
        <rect class="fig-box fig-box-slow" x="70" y="124" width="180" height="36" rx="8"/>
        <text class="fig-box-text" x="160" y="147" text-anchor="middle">retrain the model</text>
        <line class="fig-flow" x1="160" y1="162" x2="160" y2="182" marker-end="url(#fig-arrow)"/>
        <rect class="fig-box" x="70" y="186" width="180" height="36" rx="8"/>
        <text class="fig-box-text" x="160" y="209" text-anchor="middle">redeploy</text>
        <path class="fig-flow fig-flow-loop" d="M250 204 H282 V80 H254" marker-end="url(#fig-arrow)"/>
        <text class="fig-label" x="296" y="138" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(90 296 138)">for every new app</text>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-warn" x="62" y="139" text-anchor="end">thousands</text>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-warn" x="62" y="152" text-anchor="end">of seconds</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="fig-panel">
      <p class="fig-panel-head is-accent">With retrieval: <span>add a few examples</span></p>
      <svg class="fig-svg" viewBox="0 0 320 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="cbr-b-t">
        <title id="cbr-b-t">Known traffic as grey clusters of points; a new app as five coloured points; a new flow joined to its three nearest coloured points; one flow far from every cluster circled as unknown.</title>
        <circle class="fig-known" cx="57.5" cy="69.2" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="57.9" cy="57.5" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="46.7" cy="59.2" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="79.3" cy="67.3" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="69.1" cy="64.7" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="41" cy="70.6" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="44.4" cy="47.5" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="70.8" cy="53.3" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="53.6" cy="79.5" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="86.4" cy="184.4" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="67.8" cy="160.3" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="71.8" cy="168.5" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="89" cy="173.5" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="70.2" cy="184.6" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="64.4" cy="173.3" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="84" cy="153.3" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="78.7" cy="185.8" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="54" cy="166.9" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="176.3" cy="41.8" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="186.2" cy="51.2" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="159.8" cy="60.2" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="187.7" cy="63" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="197" cy="55.8" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="163.8" cy="45.8" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="190.5" cy="36.2" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="163.6" cy="36.7" r="4"/><circle class="fig-known" cx="175.3" cy="64.2" r="4"/>
        <text class="fig-label" x="18" y="112">known apps</text>
        <circle class="fig-new" cx="226" cy="150" r="4.5"/><circle class="fig-new" cx="240" cy="163" r="4.5"/><circle class="fig-new" cx="219" cy="170" r="4.5"/><circle class="fig-new" cx="248" cy="147" r="4.5"/><circle class="fig-new" cx="233" cy="182" r="4.5"/>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-new" x="262" y="140">new app</text>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-new" x="262" y="153">5 flows added</text>
        <line class="fig-link" x1="208" y1="196" x2="219" y2="170"/><line class="fig-link" x1="208" y1="196" x2="233" y2="182"/><line class="fig-link" x1="208" y1="196" x2="240" y2="163"/>
        <circle class="fig-query" cx="208" cy="196" r="5.5"/>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-strong" x="106" y="226">new flow takes the label</text>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-strong" x="106" y="239">of its nearest neighbours</text>
        <circle class="fig-radius" cx="290" cy="92" r="17"/>
        <circle class="fig-unknown" cx="290" cy="92" r="5.5"/>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-warn" x="314" y="60" text-anchor="end">far from everything:</text>
        <text class="fig-label fig-label-warn" x="314" y="73" text-anchor="end">flagged as unknown</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    A retrieval classifier keeps a map of flows it has seen. Teaching it a new app means dropping a few labelled flows into the map, which takes
    seconds; a retrained model takes thousands. A flow far from every known app is flagged as unknown in the same step.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
